#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279907 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa65a73-e750-5052-9249-7c096297ae51" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Value of a Minor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fcec5bf5-c244-5346-a821-261d6fd2baa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279909} {:answer/id #uuid "9d382f75-3cf3-500a-a4bd-ca561f8516bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcec5bf5-c244-5346-a821-261d6fd2baa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279909} :answer-field/id #uuid "562568b5-fbbd-5a72-b8c7-51736263fa19" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279908} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db4b9131-5fa9-552a-ba5b-692e5cfc1451" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db4b9131-5fa9-552a-ba5b-692e5cfc1451" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279912} :answer-field/id #uuid "42c56cc1-6826-5ee1-9aee-341d32eb0613" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279911}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "11118463-734f-544a-8796-95bbe47cd463" :question/math-academy-id "q-275530" :question/problem "Given that the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is $17$, find all the possible values of $p$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & p & 4 \\\\ 6 & -2 & p\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **ascending order**, the values of $p$ are\n\n$p=$ \n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and $\\,p=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the minor of ${a}_{11},$ we remove the first row and first column:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & p & 4 \\\\ ∗ & -2 & p\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}p & 4 \\\\ -2 & p\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}p & 4 \\\\ -2 & p\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =p\\cdot p-4\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & ={p}^{2}+8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is $17$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{2}+8 & =17 \\\\ {p}^{2}-9 & =0 \\\\ (p-3)(p+3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $p=-3$ and $p=3.$"}]}
